1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Messages organizes departmental notices
into Inbox, Sent, and All Messages.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Chat organizes ongoing conversations.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,800
Choose the audience and purpose
before composing anything.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,400
Community response teams can use a
notice for a briefing and a chat for

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,800
coordination; industrial teams can use
the same distinction for shift handovers.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:23,600
A stored message in your own app
confirms a record, not delivery

7
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,200
to every recipient’s device.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,600
The Compose icon opens New Message.

9
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:32,800
Choose Message Type and Recipients, then
enter a clear Subject and Message Body.

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,000
The recipient picker separates
People, Groups, and Roles.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,400
Check the selected names before Send.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,400
Our training notice goes only
to the fictional Boden account.

13
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:48,400
Find its saved card in Sent and open
the content afterward; do not treat that

14
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,200
card as proof of a push notification.

15
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:56,000
An incoming Poll can open Respond
to Message through its reply arrow.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Enter Response, add a Note
(Optional), and choose Send Response.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,400
The training polls show a
stored Yes response as code one;

18
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,000
inspect the Responded result.

19
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,200
Long-pressing a card exposes
Select All and Delete.

20
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,800
Review the selection carefully.

21
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:14,800
This browser’s native confirmation
does not complete deletion, so these

22
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,400
examples preserve both messages.

23
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:21,200
Open New conversation and choose
New Direct Message for one person or

24
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,600
New Group for a shared discussion.

25
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:27,200
Search for the intended member
instead of choosing Everyone.

26
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:32,400
Name the group and review the selected
people before you create the group.

27
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:36,000
Direct messages, channels, and
incidents then organize the list.

28
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,600
SAR task teams and security posts can
use these same audience checks to avoid

29
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,000
sending coordination to the wrong team.

30
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,600
Confirm the conversation name
before entering Type a message.

31
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:53,200
Attach is the plus icon; its menu
offers Emoji, Add image, Add GIF, Share

32
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,600
location, and Urgent in a channel.

33
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,000
Send is the paper-plane icon and
becomes available after entering text.

34
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Threads offer fewer attachment choices.

35
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,600
This exercise uses fictional text;
media services, location permissions,

36
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,600
and real hardware require separate
checks on the intended platform.

37
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,400
Long-press a message
to inspect its actions.

38
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:16,799
The training account’s own-message
menu shows Reply in thread, Copy, Edit,

39
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:18,799
Delete, Pin, and moderator removal.

40
00:02:18,799 --> 00:02:21,600
Available actions depend on
ownership and permissions.

41
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:26,000
Thread keeps the ORIGINAL MESSAGE
visible while you add related replies.

42
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,600
Review the target before editing,
pinning, deleting, or moderating.

43
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:33,200
The captured reply is fictional;
no deletion or moderator

44
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,400
removal is demonstrated.

45
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:39,200
Assistant opens a question workspace
with New session and a Send icon.

46
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:44,800
Decide what you need to know and whether
the information is approved for that

47
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,400
service before submitting anything.

48
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:50,800
A bounded question about a training
procedure is more useful than

49
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,800
a vague request for everything.

50
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:57,200
This recording stays on the
workspace: it does not invoke a

51
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,200
provider or validate an answer.

52
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:02,000
Verify any operational answer
against approved references.

53
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,600
Voice opens Voice Channels.

54
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:07,200
This training configuration says
No voice channels available, so

55
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,000
there is no channel to join here.

56
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,200
Resolve that setup before
relying on voice coordination.

57
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:17,200
A configured deployment also needs the
intended device’s audio permissions,

58
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:20,800
microphone, and push-to-talk equipment
checked through an approved test.

59
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:25,200
An empty browser list cannot establish
native radio or background-audio behavior.

60
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:28,000
Keep the team’s agreed fallback
communication available.

61
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,200
Stream opens Audio Streams
and Select Audio Stream.

62
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:36,000
None means no stream is selected;
the screen also says no audio

63
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,600
stream is currently playing.

64
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:40,000
Refresh Streams reloads
the configured list.

65
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,600
In Settings, BT Handset currently
says No device selected.

66
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,000
Inspect these states before
troubleshooting audio.

67
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Browser settings do not demonstrate
Bluetooth pairing, headset buttons, or

68
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,800
native background playback, and this
exercise does not connect a real provider.

69
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,600
Contacts opens Contact
Details with Details, Notes,

70
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,200
Pre-Plan, Files, and Calls.

71
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:02,400
Confirm the contact’s identity
before following its information.

72
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:06,000
Our fictional warehouse has no
recorded preplan, notes, files,

73
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,400
or related calls in these tabs.

74
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:12,800
That absence does not establish
that the site has no hazards.

75
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:17,600
Wildland and industrial teams can
use the same tabs for reliable access

76
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:21,600
information and site documents once
their department has populated them.

77
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,400
Notes contains the Firehouse
51 — shift briefing.

78
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:29,600
Open it to read the actual briefing
content and its category and date.

79
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:33,200
Protocols is a separate reference
library; this training department

80
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,800
shows No protocols found.

81
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:38,800
Search the appropriate library and
confirm that an approved reference

82
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,800
exists before relying on it.

83
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:45,200
Reading a briefing does not
create a protocol, and an empty

84
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:49,200
library is a reason to obtain the
correct departmental material.

85
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:52,400
In Settings, inspect Keep Alive,
Realtime Geolocation, Background

86
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:54,000
Geolocation, and BT Handset.

87
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,599
These preferences affect different
device capabilities; do not assume

88
00:04:57,599 --> 00:05:00,000
one switch enables all field behavior.

89
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,200
Native background location, audio
hardware, and push notifications

90
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:07,200
require the appropriate platform,
permissions, and an approved device test.

91
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:10,400
This browser exercise leaves
the location switches off.

92
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:14,000
Confirm actual alert receipt
separately before a team depends

93
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
on a device for notifications.


